+Vault + ExternalSecrets guidance for Aegis (QPU + approver + adapters)
+
+Overview:
+- Store all QPU provider credentials in HashiCorp Vault (don't bake keys in images).
+- Use ExternalSecrets (external-secrets.io) or Vault Agent Injector to mount short-lived secrets into pods.
+- Use Kubernetes ServiceAccount to authenticate to Vault via Kubernetes auth and map roles to secrets.
+
+Quick steps:
+1. Create Vault policy (see vault-policy-examples.hcl).
+2. Enable Kubernetes auth in Vault and map k8s service accounts to Vault roles.
+3. Create secrets at paths like secret/data/quantum/ibmq and secret/data/quantum/braket.
+4. Deploy ExternalSecret manifests (see k8s/quantum/externalsecret_ibmq.yaml).
+5. Ensure adapters read secrets from ephemeral mount /var/secrets/<provider>/token or via env injected secret.
+
+Security notes:
+- Use Vault TTLs and renewals; prefer short-lived tokens.
+- Audit Vault access with Vault audit devices (file/syslog).
+- Never commit secrets or KMS URIs to git.
+
