+Cosign + Rekor wiring notes
+
+Goals:
+- Sign evidence bundles with cosign using a KMS-backed key (AWS/GCP/Azure).
+- Record the signature in Rekor transparency log.
+
+Example cosign KMS URI (AWS):
+ - "kms://arn:aws:kms:us-west-2:123456789012:key/abcd-..."
+
+Basic sign + upload flow:
+  cosign sign-blob --key ${COSIGN_KEY} <bundle.json>
+  # signature file will be <bundle.json>.sig
+  rekor-cli upload --artifact <bundle.json> --signature <bundle.json>.sig --public-key <pubkey>
+
+Automate in CI: use CI runner with cosign installed and KMS permission to sign; store COSIGN_KEY URI in GitHub Actions secrets.
