+# Canary Playbook for promoting autonomy namespace
+
+Prereqs:
+- All above components deployed (Vault, ExternalSecrets, Approver Postgres, cosign KMS, Rekor, OPA, qpu queue)
+- Monitoring (Prometheus + Grafana) online
+
+Steps:
+1. Create AutonomyMode CR for namespace:
+   kubectl apply -f k8s/autonomy/autonomy-mode-cr.yaml  # set mode to SANDBOX for canary namespace
+2. Run sandbox canary (Argo):
+   argo submit --watch ops/automation/argo_autonomy_approval_workflow.yaml -p plan-file=ops/ci/sample_plan_sandbox.json -p namespace=sandbox-ns
+3. Monitor Prometheus queries during canary:
+   - aegis_agent_safety_violations_total
+   - aegis_blocked_tool_calls_total
+   - retrain_guard_denies_total
+4. Inspect evidence bundles, cosign signatures, and Rekor entries:
+   - ls /path/to/evidence
+   - rekor-cli search --artifact <bundle.json>
+5. If stable for 24–72h, promote to HYBRID and run extended canary (ops/ci/autonomy_tests.yml)
+6. For promotion to AUTONOMOUS, run 7+ day canary and red-team tests, then follow runbook to flip mode.
+
+Rollback:
+- kubectl patch autonomymode <name> -p '{"spec":{"mode":"OFF"}}' --type=merge
+- Revoke agent SA tokens and rotate approver keys.
